---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Longer bio and background."
  currentPath="/about"
>
  <section class="content-body">
    <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1>Longer Bio</h1>
    <p>
      I build things and follow ideas wherever they go — usually software or
      hardware, but not always.
    </p>
    <p>
      I’m interested in technology, art, and philosophy, and how they show up in
      the things I make.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site is a collection of projects, notes, and experiments along the way.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most of what I build lives on a subdomain of byah.org (deckforge.byah.org,
      slopyard.byah.org, and so on) instead of its own domain name. That's on purpose. I
      miss the version of the internet where you'd stumble into someone's weird little
      corner of it just by clicking around — before everything worth visiting needed its
      own brand and its own domain. Buying a new domain for every project nudges you
      toward having fewer, more "serious" things, instead of a lot of small, unfinished,
      honest ones. Subdomains keep that friction low and put everything under one roof I
      actually maintain, so I'd rather add another link under byah.org than register
      another .com. (<a href="/projects/landlordlog/">landlordlog</a> is the exception —
      that one has its own domain and might end up fully standalone.)
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
